## 3. Package Naming: **monoterminal.v1** Confirmed

Use `package monoterminal.v1;` exactly as specified.

Generated Rust module path will be: `monoterminal::v1::{Envelope, AttachRequest, ...}`

---

## 4. Build Setup Details

**File structure:**
```
proto/
  monoterminal/
    v1/
      messages.proto    ← Your schema file

crates/protocol/
  build.rs             ← prost-build configuration
  Cargo.toml
  src/
    lib.rs             ← Re-export generated types
```

**build.rs:**
```rust
// crates/protocol/build.rs
fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
    prost_build::Config::new()
        .out_dir("src/generated")
        .compile_protos(
            &["../../proto/monoterminal/v1/messages.proto"],
            &["../../proto"],
        )?;
    Ok(())
}
```

**Cargo.toml:**
```toml
[package]
name = "monoterminal-protocol"
# ... (workspace metadata)

[dependencies]
prost = { workspace = true }
bytes = "1"

[build-dependencies]
prost-build = { workspace = true }
```

